---
/*
  A PHOTOGRAPH AND A PASSAGE, SHARING ONE SCREEN (2026-08-11, section 82).

  WHY THIS EXISTS. The site had screens of pure text, and at 1440 a paragraph
  sat in a 640px column with the rest of the screen empty. Both attempts to fix
  it by spacing failed: pinned left it read as an afterthought, and centred it
  put the spine in the middle of an empty screen with dead space either side.

  Then the four references were re-measured for RUNNING PROSE specifically, and
  the answer was not a spacing value:

    Rick Owens    no brand prose on the home page at all. The only 120+
                  character run is the cookie banner.
    Sorcinelli    the same. One 22px statement, over a full-screen slideshow.
    Sellam        ONE block, 396 characters, 17.9px, CENTRED, tucked directly
                  under a full-bleed photograph with ~60px of air.
    Ferdressed    no brand prose. The long runs are shipping and returns policy.

  **A column of words alone on flat ground appears nowhere in any of them.**
  Text is over a photograph, or hard against one, or it is a single short line
  holding a screen. So the fault was never the margin: it was that these
  sections were SEQUENCED between photographs instead of COMPOSED with them.

  WHAT THIS DOES. At desktop the photograph takes one half of a full screen and
  the passage takes the other, so neither is ever alone and the text gets a
  measure by construction — half of 1440 less its padding is about 560px, inside
  the readable band without any capping.

  On a phone NOTHING CHANGES: the photograph is a full-bleed frame and the text
  is a surface under it, exactly the stack that already worked. This is a
  desktop composition, not a new layout.

  THE SEAM IS THE STRUCTURE. Where the photograph meets the text is a real edge
  in the composition, which is why the spine is not drawn here: a hairline
  floating beside a photograph's edge would be two lines saying one thing. See
  the note on Spine for what the spine is now.
*/
import MediaSurface from "./MediaSurface.astro";
import type {MediaItem} from "../lib/media";
import type {Locale} from "../lib/locales";

interface Props {
  media: MediaItem | null;
  locale: Locale;
  /** Which side the photograph takes at desktop. Alternate down a page. */
  side?: "left" | "right";
  class?: string;
}

const {media, locale, side = "left", class: className = ""} = Astro.props;
---

{
  media ? (
    <section class:list={["paired", side === "right" && "paired-flip", className]}>
      <div class="paired-media">
        <MediaSurface media={media} locale={locale} height="paired" sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 50vw, 100vw" />
      </div>
      <div class="paired-text">
        <div class="paired-inner">
          <slot />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  ) : (
    /* No photograph: the passage stands on its own surface exactly as before. */
    <section class="paired paired-alone frame">
      <div class="paired-inner">
        <slot />
      </div>
    </section>
  )
}
